argus (1.0.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New collect-crowdsec.sh: counts CrowdSec alerts per scenario via
    `cscli alerts list -o json` + jq, same auto-detect/no-op-if-absent
    pattern as collect-fail2ban.sh — both backends can run at once.
    UNTESTED against a real CrowdSec instance (never had one available this
    cycle); treat as best-effort until confirmed against a live install.
  * plot.sh/plot.gp renamed chart-daily.sh/chart-daily.gp — a future
    hour-of-day view needs its own name, "plot" doesn't scale to more than
    one chart type.
  * chart-daily: two regressions found by comparing against real historical
    charts (2024/2025/2026) fixed — numeric value labels on every point
    (were present since 2025, silently dropped in 1.0.0-1) restored; colour
    per series now resolved by name (stable across years) instead of by
    discovery position (was changing the same series' colour year to year).
  * New config knobs in /etc/argus/argus.conf: ARGUS_IMG_WIDTH/HEIGHT (chart
    size), ARGUS_LANG (fr/en, resolves the chart's own title and axis
    labels — not just a future separate report), ARGUS_COULEUR_<name>
    (explicit colour override per series, hyphens in jail names sanitised
    to underscores for the variable name — a hard bash constraint, hyphens
    are not valid in shell identifiers).
  * Legacy 2024 scripts fully removed from the repository (not just
    untracked) — copy preserved in the private _CADRE archive, never
    published. scripts/preflight-publication.sh moved out of the public
    repository entirely (maintainer-only tool, zero value to someone
    installing Argus).

 -- Ronan Davalan <ronan@davalan.fr>  Wed, 22 Jul 2026 14:13:01 +0200

argus (1.0.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * collect-ssh.sh: journald fallback (systemd unit "ssh", overridable via
    ARGUS_SSHD_UNIT), used automatically when auth.log is absent — Debian
    13 minimal installs without rsyslog have no auth.log at all, only
    journald, discovered on a real install (Davalan-vps). Both sources feed
    the same threshold logic through a common intermediate format
    ("<date> <heure> <ip>"); no configuration needed, no functional
    difference in the "not every failed login is an attack" rule.
    Validated end-to-end against real journald data (52 raw failed
    attempts correctly extracted).

 -- Ronan Davalan <ronan@davalan.fr>  Tue, 21 Jul 2026 17:30:12 +0200

argus (1.0.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Storage moved from /var/lib/argus (correct FHS for internal program
    state, but requires root/sudo to retrieve anything) to /srv/argus (FHS:
    "data served by this system") — root:root 755, world-readable files.
    Validated by a real install on a second machine (Davalan-vps) that
    surfaced this as a genuine retrieval problem, not a style preference.
  * Dropped the "argus" system group entirely — it only existed to work
    around /var/lib's restriction; nothing Argus writes is sensitive (no
    individual IP address, ever), so nothing justifies gating reads behind
    a group. debian/postinst and postrm simplified accordingly (no more
    addgroup/delgroup).
  * New optional ARGUS_DATA_OWNER setting (/etc/argus/argus.conf): when set,
    collect-ssh.sh, collect-fail2ban.sh and plot.sh chown their output to
    that user after writing, so charts land directly in an operator's own
    home directory, actually owned by them — not just world-readable under
    /srv. Collection itself keeps running as root via cron regardless
    (reliable independently of whether that user can read auth.log/
    fail2ban.log on a given machine).
  * README: retrieval documented as rsync/scp run by the operator, no push
    or notification mechanism — rsync recommended as the primary pattern
    (builds an accumulating local mirror, consistent with the
    unlimited-horizon argument).

 -- Ronan Davalan <ronan@davalan.fr>  Tue, 21 Jul 2026 17:18:04 +0200

argus (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial public release. Standalone SSH attack counter reading auth.log
    directly (collect-ssh.sh, threshold-based: a source IP counts as one
    attack per day once it crosses ARGUS_SSH_THRESHOLD failed attempts,
    default 5 — not every failed login). Optional Fail2Ban jail counter
    (collect-fail2ban.sh), auto-detected, reuses Fail2Ban's own ban
    decisions instead of re-implementing detection.
  * Storage: flat text files, one per year per source, hourly-bucketed
    ("<count> <date>Thour>") — deliberate choice to avoid database
    corruption risk over a multi-year horizon, and to make an hour/day-of-
    week breakdown possible later without any new collection (deferred to
    v1.1+, see SPECIFICATIONS/V1_0_0_PUBLICATION.md in the private _CADRE).
  * plot.sh aggregates the hourly buckets to daily totals, then renders via
    plot.gp — adapted from the original 2024 gnuplot script (unlimited
    historical horizon, dynamic multi-series discovery), otherwise
    unchanged.
  * Never stores or displays individual attacker IP addresses — daily counts
    only, since the project's inception in 2024.

 -- Ronan Davalan <ronan@davalan.fr>  Tue, 21 Jul 2026 14:14:49 +0200
